  "id": "glycolysis",
  "name": "Glycolysis",
  "category": "metabolic",
  "topic": "metabolism",
  "summary": "Ten cytosolic reactions split one glucose (C6) into two pyruvate (C3). The preparatory phase invests 2 ATP; the payoff phase (run twice per glucose) yields 4 ATP and 2 NADH.",
  "evidence": "established",
  "layout": "chain",
  "location": "Cytosol",
  "net": "Glucose + 2 NAD⁺ + 2 ADP + 2 Pᵢ → 2 Pyruvate + 2 NADH + 2 H⁺ + 2 ATP + 2 H₂O",
  "clinical": "Cancer cells upregulate glycolysis even with oxygen (Warburg effect), the basis of ¹⁸F-FDG PET imaging. Pyruvate kinase deficiency causes haemolytic anaemia; red cells rely entirely on glycolysis.",
